  "interpretation": "G_model measures how reliably the evaluation design distinguishes between models. Under the full design (6 prompts \u00d7 6 seeds \u00d7 2 temps \u00d7 4 orderings \u00d7 200 items), G_model ranges from 0.6708 (ARC) to 0.9576 (HellaSwag). ARC and GSM8K have low G_model primarily because model\u00d7prompt interaction is very large (88% and 92% of relative error respectively), meaning prompt template choice substantially changes model rankings. HellaSwag and MATH achieve G_model > 0.95, indicating robust model differentiation. Contrast with G_item (0.86\u20130.90 across all benchmarks): item difficulty measurement is consistently reliable, but model ranking reliability varies dramatically by benchmark. The practical implication: for benchmarks with large model\u00d7prompt interactions (ARC, GSM8K), single-prompt evaluations cannot reliably rank models."
